comments.body:
@nemeth-it @markjaquith I missed that feature, too.
So I created a fork of Ice for myself and implemented everything I wanted. I wanted the code cleaned up and a Swift 6 code base and many other things. I did it for myself, but if anyone else finds it useful, you're welcome to use it too. It's only the 971st fork anyway 😉

https://github.com/holzcloud/holzBar

@jordanbaird Now it is possible to drag and drop items in settings. I’m running version 0.10.5.

One thing, when you navigate the list of apps in the settings, VoiceOver says: «layout item». However, when I invoke help menu on each object by pressing VO key (⌃⌥) + ⇧ + H, I get to know the name of the app.

Is it possible for you to swap those two, that when you browsing the list, VoiceOver should announce app names instead of layout item?

@jonpurdy YESSSSSSSS that is exactly what I have in mind, thank you for the visual - I think it's very effective in conveying the value and ease of use of such a feature. 

It doesn't even need to enable any functions directly from the dropdown menu - it would be good enough if making a selection from this list just temporarily exposes the app icon in the menu bar. At least then I can be sure it's actually in the menubar, and I have a fresh reminder of which icon to select. 

This also works as a great way to monitor/measure all the various menubar apps running in a system, which is otherwise challenging when gauging off icons alone.
